##: {{ux|en|I was '''after''' finishing my dinner when there was a knock on the door. ''[''{{=}} I had just finished my dinner when ...'']''}}
##* {{quote-book|en|title=Evenings in the Duffrey|page=283|author=Patrick Kennedy|year=1875|passage=He '''was after''' walking on the Thursday, Friday, and Saturday before, all the way from the County Limerick, where his brother, Father John, has a parish; and you may believe, the poor man was tired}}
##* {{quote-journal|en|journal=The Shanachie|title=A Miracle Play|author={{w|Augusta, Lady Gregory|Lady Gregory}}|volume=1|year=1906|passage=Mother: Let him get away out of this now, himself and his share of songs. Look at the way he has your bib destroyed that I '''was after''' washing in the morning!}}
##* {{quote-book|en|title=Star of the Sea|page=40|author=Joseph O'Connor|year=2004|passage=When I woke up it was black-dark and the music '''was after''' stopping. I could taste the bread I '''was after''' eating in the dream, as sweet and luscious as any I ever knew|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=uClSqONkcW0C&pg=PA40&dq=%22be%7Cwas%7Cam%7Care%7Cis%7Cwere%7Cbeen%7Cbeing+after+washing%7Ccleaning%7Cfinishing%7Ceating%22&hl=en&ei=lnZBTuv7POfy0gGez5HKCQ&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=21&ved=0CIsBEOgBMBQ4eA#v=onepage&q=%22be%7Cwas%7Cam%7Care%7Cis%7Cwere%7Cbeen%7Cbeing%20after%20washing%7Ccleaning%7Cfinishing%7Ceating%22&f=false}}
##* {{quote-book|en|title=Longarm and the Great Milk Train Robbery|author=Tabor Evans|year=2004|passage=He asked directions to the dairy those milk cans had shown up late at. Corrigan pointed back the way he'd come and explained, “You'd '''have been after''' riding past their loading platform because they don't have their sign overlooking where the train would '''be after''' stopping.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|title=The Black Box|page=45|author=M. P. Shiel|year=2008|passage="Yes. And where were ''you'' when the flood broke loose?" / "I would be most of the way to the Old House then. O'Loughlin '''was after''' running in wild to tell me he was hearing the Banshee out at The Old House, {{...}}."}}
